@startuml 04-runtime-console-qml
!pragma layout smetana
' 运行时责任 3/4：输出、输入桥接与 QML 呈现
' 来源：eraengine.cpp, GameProc/execution_engine.h, GameView/console_backend.h,
'       GameView/system_status_manager.h, GameView/input_handler.h, qml/Console.qml,
'       qml/ConsoleInput.qml

title 运行时：控制台与 QML 展示链

package "GameProc" {
  class ExecutionEngine {
    .. output signals ..
    + consolePrint(text, newline)
    + consoleReuseLastLine(text)
    + consolePrintTemplate(output)
    + requestAnyKey()
    .. Template IR is built during load ..
    .. runtime fills Expression placeholders ..
    .. IR is reused only while verifiable ..
    .. += of a string value drops verified ..
    .. dynamic full strings reuse the same lexer once ..
    .. compileMarkup is the single HTML tokenizer ..
    + consolePrintButton(text, intValue, strValue, isString)
    + clearTextBox()
  }

  class ScriptRunner {
    .. input signals ..
    + inputRequested(kind, defaultValue)
    + suspended(state)
  }

  class EraEngine {
    + provideInput(value)
    + provideInputString(value)
    + provideMouseKey(type, r1, r2, r3, r4)
    + executeConsoleCommand(text)
    .. Q_PROPERTY console / statusManager / inputHandler ..
  }

  class SystemStatusManager {
    + onScriptStarted(script)
    + onScriptFinished()
    + onError(message)
    + onStateChanged(state)
    .. statusChanged() ..
  }
}

package "GameView" {
  class ConsoleBackend <<QAbstractListModel>> {
    + inputKind : QString
    + waitingInput : bool
    + anyKeyInput : bool
    + stringInput : bool
    + oneInput : bool
    + framePacingAttached : bool
    + lineModel / historyModel / stageModel
    + notifyInputRequested(kind, defaultValue)
    + notifyInputCommitted()
    + submitInput(value)
    + submitInputString(value)
    + submitAnyKey()
    + submitMouseKey(...)
    + notifyFramePresented()
    + markDirty()
    + flush()
    + tick()
    .. inputRequested(kind) ..
    .. inputSubmitted(value) ..
    .. inputSubmittedString(value) ..
    .. presentationRequested() ..
    .. framePresented() ..
    .. generationChanged() ..
  }

  class InputHandler {
    + setInputResult(result)
    + waitForInput() : int
  }

  note right of ScriptRunner
    INPUT / ONEINPUT and INPUTS / ONEINPUTS keep comma positions.
    The first field is the default value; an empty first field means
    no default and must not consume the second field. String-family
    defaults use FORM semantics: a bare token is literal text, while
    an unresolved integer default is a load-time error. The runner
    owns this field mapping; QML only submits the resulting value.
  end note
}

package "QML" {
  class QmlConsole
  class QmlInput
  class QmlMain

  note right of QmlConsole
    backend : ConsoleBackend
    generationChanged -> capture
    presentationRequested -> syncView / positionStage
    Qt.callLater -> syncView / positionStage -> backend.notifyFramePresented()
    The callback acknowledges model/layout work;
    it does not prove a scene-graph swap or pixels on screen.
  end note

  note right of QmlInput
    submit()
    submitText(text)
    handleTextEdited()
    TextField.onAccepted
    TextField.onTextEdited
  end note

  note right of QmlMain
    eraEngine : EraEngine
    contains Console and ConsoleInput
  end note
}

ExecutionEngine ..> EraEngine : Qt signals
ScriptRunner ..> EraEngine : inputRequested
EraEngine --> ConsoleBackend : print / notify input
ConsoleBackend ..> EraEngine : submitted input
EraEngine --> SystemStatusManager : state and execution signals
EraEngine --> InputHandler : QML-owned compatibility input
QmlMain *-- QmlConsole
QmlMain *-- QmlInput
QmlConsole --> ConsoleBackend : models / properties
QmlInput --> ConsoleBackend : submit*()
ConsoleBackend ..> QmlConsole : presentationRequested / framePresented

note right of ConsoleBackend
  ConsoleBackend is the single convergence point for input:
  integer, string, any-key, mouse-key and button paths all
  finish by ending the wait and emitting one submission signal.
  QML reads inputKind/waitingInput and never infers the kind
  from a SystemStateCode.
end note

note top of ExecutionEngine
  HTML path has one tokenizer (compileMarkup) and two entry points:
  load-time compile() for the provable skeleton, and print-time
  parseRuntimeMarkup() for the final value. A value keeps its IR
  (verified=true) only when that IR came from scanning the whole value
  once. concatenateStrings() always drops the flag: a tag can straddle
  two separately scanned pieces (eraTW prints `<font ...>` and
  `</font>` from two `+=` lines), so pairing cannot be proven.
  coversText() then reports the value as uncovered and the print
  re-runs the same lexer over the final string.

  Structure problems (UnexpectedCloseTag / UnclosedTag) follow the
  same split. The lexer only records them on the IR; who reports them
  depends on who holds the final string. Load time may report them
  only for a verified template of an HTML_PRINT argument, because
  that IR is the whole value and every execution reproduces it --
  a static fact. That includes a `+=` chain rebuilt by reverse
  tracing: the chain becomes one PLUS tree at load time, so its
  skeleton (literals plus opaque expression holes) is the whole
  string and is tokenized once. A chain broken by control flow or a
  call cannot be rebuilt; its value only exists at print time.
  Tracing stops at ordinary control-flow, loops, calls, scope breaks,
  and unknown writes (policy flag kTraceAcrossControlFlow = false).
  A narrow IF/ELSE exception is proven path-wise: every branch writes
  the target and keeps the same ordered HTML skeleton; parameter-only
  differences become local IfNode holes, and the merged result becomes
  the new definition base. Missing ELSE, ELSEIF, structural tag
  differences, nested/unknown paths, and empty/ambiguous writes stop
  and preserve the variable AST for print-time evaluation. Loops remain
  conservative: unknown iteration counts stop, while a future bounded
  analysis may prove zero/one iterations. How many stopped, and the first stop, are
  logged at load so the policy can be revisited with numbers. Any dynamic value is checked at print time, where
  the final string exists (ExecutionEngine::reportMarkupProblems,
  deduplicated per source position). A fragment such as a lone
  `</font>` is unbalanced on its own, so reporting it at load would
  be a false positive.
end note

note bottom of QmlConsole
  generationChanged invalidates stale buttons and drives capture.
  presentationRequested is a layout acknowledgement handshake:
  QML synchronizes models and stage geometry, then calls
  notifyFramePresented(). This signal does not establish that Qt Quick
  has swapped a scene graph frame or that pixels reached the display.
end note

note bottom of ConsoleBackend
  Style stack is per print call: an EndStyle closes exactly one
  matching top-of-stack tag. A mismatched or unknown closing tag is
  consumed without popping, so later text cannot inherit the wrong
  font/color. Styles never leak into the next print call.
  markDirty() starts the frame timer only while a publish is pending;
  flush() stops it after the clean snapshot is emitted. tick() therefore
  has no idle 16 ms wakeups and only delegates dirty work to flush().
end note

legend bottom
  ConsoleBackend owns console state; QML owns view composition;
  EraEngine owns cross-layer signal wiring; SystemStatusManager owns status state.
endlegend
@enduml
